Troubleshoot and fix an oversized Docker build context issue caused by a missing `.dockerignore` file.

Requirements:
- Located in `/app`, you will find `app.py`, `Dockerfile`, and large directories (`build_cache/`, `node_modules/`, `.git/`).
- Notice that building the image (`docker build -t myapp:latest /app`) sends a huge build context (over 150 MB) to the Docker daemon.
- Diagnose why the build context is so large:
  - Check if a `.dockerignore` file exists in `/app` (`ls -la /app`).
  - Estimate directory sizes using `du -sh /app/*`.
- Create `/app/.dockerignore` and configure it to exclude unnecessary build artifacts and dependencies:
  ```text
  .git
  node_modules
  build_cache
  *.bin
  *.log
  ```
- Rebuild the image (`docker build -t myapp:latest /app`).
- Verify that the build context sent to the Docker daemon is small, and `/app/.dockerignore` excludes large binary files from the built image.
